1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,760
Your best ideas happen in the shower and die before you sit down.

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:07,360
Let's fix that in 10 seconds with something already on your phone.

3
00:00:07,360 --> 00:00:10,240
This is brain dump, a single iPhone shortcut,

4
00:00:10,240 --> 00:00:14,640
tap it, talk, and it saves a timestamped markdown file straight to iCloud.

5
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:17,359
No app, no subscription, no sign up.

6
00:00:17,359 --> 00:00:20,800
Just the shortcuts app you've been ignoring since 2018.

7
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:23,199
Let's build it from zero, right now.

8
00:00:23,199 --> 00:00:28,560
New shortcut, tap the plus, search, dictate text, add it.

9
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:31,520
This fires up your mic and transcribes everything you say in real time.

10
00:00:32,160 --> 00:00:36,160
Here's the thing, under stop listening, set it to after pause.

11
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:38,480
That means it records until you stop talking.

12
00:00:39,359 --> 00:00:43,920
5 seconds, fine, 5 minutes, also fine, it just waits.

13
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:46,240
Rename the shortcut brain dump at the top.

14
00:00:46,240 --> 00:00:49,120
Throw a brain emoji on there because we're adults.

15
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:50,800
Okay, so now we have raw text.

16
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:52,960
But raw text with no timestamp is a junk drawer.

17
00:00:52,960 --> 00:00:54,000
Let's fix that.

18
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:56,320
Next, add current date.

19
00:00:56,399 --> 00:00:58,880
This grabs the exact moment you run the shortcut.

20
00:00:59,520 --> 00:01:02,719
But the default format is not great for file names.

21
00:01:02,719 --> 00:01:05,120
So right below it, add format date.

22
00:01:05,680 --> 00:01:08,719
Switch from short to custom and type this exact string.

23
00:01:09,280 --> 00:01:16,480
yyyy-MM-dd-HHmm.

24
00:01:16,480 --> 00:01:18,960
That's the format string.

25
00:01:19,840 --> 00:01:22,480
Look, I know that sounds like a regex incantation.

26
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:25,840
But it gives you year-month, day-hour minute.

27
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:27,600
Clean, sortable.

28
00:01:27,600 --> 00:01:28,720
Obsidian, friendly.

29
00:01:28,720 --> 00:01:33,840
If your preview says something like 2026-04-10-1131, you nailed it.

30
00:01:33,840 --> 00:01:36,160
This becomes your file name. Don't skip it.

31
00:01:36,160 --> 00:01:39,680
Now we build the file body add a text action, tap inside.

32
00:01:39,680 --> 00:01:42,320
Grab dictated text from the variables bar.

33
00:01:42,320 --> 00:01:43,600
That blue pill?

34
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:44,800
That's everything you said.

35
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,320
Transcribed in one block.

36
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,520
Done.

37
00:01:47,520 --> 00:01:49,200
Now, save file.

38
00:01:49,200 --> 00:01:51,360
Set the destination to iCloud Drive.

39
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:55,280
I put mine in a folder called journal_inbox.

40
00:01:55,359 --> 00:01:57,200
Think of it as a landing zone.

41
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,920
Raw brain dumps pile up here until you process them.

42
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:02,799
Folder doesn't exist yet, doesn't matter.

43
00:02:02,799 --> 00:02:04,560
Shortcuts creates it on first run.

44
00:02:05,359 --> 00:02:06,960
Here's the key move, toggle off.

45
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,639
Ask where to save.

46
00:02:09,520 --> 00:02:10,879
You want zero friction.

47
00:02:10,879 --> 00:02:14,080
Tap talk, done, no dialogs, no decisions.

48
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:19,599
Almost there, add, rename, because text.txt tells you nothing six months from now.

49
00:02:19,599 --> 00:02:20,879
Set input to saved file.

50
00:02:21,520 --> 00:02:24,080
For the name, grab your formatted date variable

51
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:26,640
then type -braindump.md.

52
00:02:27,200 --> 00:02:30,640
So you get something like 2026-04-10,

53
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:32,880
1131-braindump.md.

54
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:34,000
Beautiful.

55
00:02:34,560 --> 00:02:40,080
That dot md extension means Obsidian, notion, any text editor, they all love it.

56
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:44,400
Last action, show notification, title, brain dump saved.

57
00:02:45,040 --> 00:02:47,600
Body dropping that same formatted date variable.

58
00:02:48,160 --> 00:02:49,840
This is your dopamine hit.

59
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:52,160
The little ping that says, yeah, it worked.

60
00:02:52,879 --> 00:02:54,479
Seven actions total.

61
00:02:54,479 --> 00:02:56,240
That's the whole shortcut.

62
00:02:56,240 --> 00:02:58,719
If you can order DoorDash, you can build this.

63
00:02:58,719 --> 00:03:00,639
Let's run it, tap brain dump.

64
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:02,079
Mic goes hot, talk.

65
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:04,479
Idea for PatchMyDay.

66
00:03:04,479 --> 00:03:08,159
Video on AI agents that process journal entries and extract action items.

67
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:11,199
I stop talking and stop listening.

68
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,400
Bam, notification, brain dump saved.

69
00:03:14,400 --> 00:03:15,439
Okay, let's verify.

70
00:03:15,439 --> 00:03:16,240
Files app.

71
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:19,519
iCloud Drive, Shortcuts, journal_inbox.

72
00:03:20,159 --> 00:03:23,120
There it is, tap it open, exact transcription.

73
00:03:23,120 --> 00:03:24,560
Already in iCloud.

74
00:03:24,560 --> 00:03:26,160
Already synced to my Mac.

75
00:03:26,160 --> 00:03:27,680
Already visible in Obsidian.

76
00:03:28,320 --> 00:03:29,120
Look at that timer.

77
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:32,080
10 seconds from thought to save file.

78
00:03:32,080 --> 00:03:33,360
You never opened an app.

79
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,920
Never typed a character, you just talked.

80
00:03:35,920 --> 00:03:37,920
Three power moves, rapid fire.

81
00:03:38,560 --> 00:03:41,600
One, long press the tile, add to home screen.

82
00:03:42,240 --> 00:03:44,080
Now it's a one-tap icon on your dock.

83
00:03:44,879 --> 00:03:46,480
I keep mine next to the camera.

84
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,600
It's that useful.

85
00:03:48,319 --> 00:03:51,280
Two, say, hey Siri, brain dump.

86
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,479
It fires hands free.

87
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,719
Perfect for driving.

88
00:03:54,719 --> 00:03:56,400
You literally never touch the phone.

89
00:03:57,359 --> 00:03:59,519
Three, and this is where it gets spicy.

90
00:03:59,519 --> 00:04:01,359
That journal inbox folder.

91
00:04:01,359 --> 00:04:04,959
It's just a directory on iCloud, which means you can point a Python script at it.

92
00:04:04,959 --> 00:04:11,039
An AI agent, a cron job that runs every night, reads your dumps, extracts action items,

93
00:04:11,039 --> 00:04:12,959
drops the summary into your task manager.

94
00:04:13,680 --> 00:04:14,799
That's not hypothetical.

95
00:04:15,359 --> 00:04:16,800
That's what I'm building next.

96
00:04:16,960 --> 00:04:19,759
Seven actions, $0, your ideas stop disappearing.

97
00:04:20,639 --> 00:04:26,160
Next video, I'm building the AI agent that actually reads these brain dumps and files action items

98
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:27,840
into a task board automatically.

99
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:31,199
It's half done, and it's kind of terrifying how well it works.

100
00:04:31,920 --> 00:04:33,360
Subscribe so you don't miss it.

101
00:04:33,360 --> 00:04:34,000
See you in that one.
